/-
Johnson/Desc/Kinds/Law/K6LawAtMgAll.lean (OF
THE PIECE IT ASKS Seated, not Object61 (Johnson/Desc/Sound/Border62.lean);
over Desc/First/PubFoot.lean): THE SHARE OF
THE SUB-PROTOCOL AT THE OUTPUT HEAD IN THE CHAIN OF PROMISES, AT THE COMPOSED MEANING OF ALL AUTHORS' PARTS "mgAll D Mg"
(Johnson/Desc/Sound/MgAll.lean: its reference form), AT THE FULL CHAIN, IN THE GOALS'
SCOPE, GENERAL IN THE PARAMETERS D, IN THE INNERMOST MEANING Mg AND IN A CONDITION Rch THAT STANDS
BESIDE THE TABLE'S PROMISE: it ends in KindTiedR D.N (mgAll D Mg) linksFull (the
driver's places) Rch (the table's extractors) l K6, UNDER NAMED PREMISES. THE STATEMENT THAT COUNTS
stands at closed terms: Law/K06Kind.lean, over Law/K06AtConst.lean: this file is what they call.

Main names (namespace VerifiableInference.Desc.Kinds.Head.Law.AtTable).
  K6DueMg ... bS numD bs q: what is left at the piece, one field a premise: 35 fields, each with its
      own line of words.
  dueAt_of_mg: K6DueMg gives Law/K6TiedAtObject.lean's structure K6DueAt at mgAll.
  kindTied_K6_mgAll: in the goals' scope (hZ, hR, hX): if the piece at number 341 is seated
      (Johnson/Desc/Sound/K6Tied.lean: Seated) and meets K6DueMg: KindTiedR ... K6 at mgAll.
  kindTied_K6_fold: the same under FoldFacts (Johnson/Desc/First/FoldFacts.lean) whole: a corollary.

THE FOLD FACTS THAT ARE SPENT, ALL UNDER Rch 341 a AND NO MARK. hfold: FoldAt Lp Mm
D.cs D.shape lay6 a.1.2 (Law/K6RestAt.lean): five sentences: FoldFacts' fields seatsCarried and
msgShapes in their own words (at its d.L, d.M), and its fields codes, liveShape, liveLayout with the
three parts of its d.sent written as D.cs, D.shape, lay6 · hreqIs: its field reqIs.

THE 35 FIELDS, SORTED.
  TESTS WITH CODE ON PUBLIC DATA: laid, planC, seatsC, namedC, callsC, maskC, roomC · blocks, book,
      fenceT · and a pair of equations: numbers.
  OTHER FACTS ON PUBLIC DATA: seg · place.
  ON THE COMPOSED MEANING'S PARAMETERS: sorts · ns · hid · head · wt · readers · uH · treesB · lay ·
      blind · more, cap · runs3, back3, runs2, back2, runsObj, back (six at one link).
  ON THE VERIFIER'S STATE AT 341: reach (under Rch alone) · tokSmall, bare, start (under the promise
      and Rch).
BESIDE THE STRUCTURE, TEN: hfold · hreqIs · hreqW (the words of the request are those of the
request that the hidden values read) · hMore (the innermost meaning's list of extra public tests is
empty) · hPP (its public sentences hold AT THE ITEMS THAT ARE OPEN AT BORDER 342 BUT THE LOOKUPS'
left AND leftOn: asked at every item, the premise would be false at
the base meaning mgBase (MgBase.lean), and the statement empty there) · hMg, hPubH, hreq (its
"in order", its public tests, and the hidden values' request, do not read where the chain stands) ·
hput (put turns the reply alone) ·
hrqX (the caller's request is the hidden values'). AND, inside hall: Seated at piece 341: the lot's
block · the piece's sub-protocol refuses more than it · its yes bears no mark · the piece holds it,
lifted over the public part · no round behind.

WHAT IS DERIVED, AND BY WHAT. The third tie's sentence behind (Law/K6OpenedCut.lean,
K6RecordAt.lean; Law/K6RestAt.lean from hfold and seatsC; Law/K6WideFront.lean from
treesB). The four items that the table's row closes: constr 24 idn (
Law/K6FourthConstr.lean) and worth 24 3 "rider", "keys", "planes" (Law/K6WorthAtMgAll.lean,
K6PlanesAtMgAll.lean, HeadWeightsMeet.lean, K6HeardOfLookOut.lean;
Law/PlanK6Planes.lean from namedC, Law/K6CallsTest.lean from callsC and maskC). The second tie
(Law/K6SecondKept.lean), with all fifteen public tests that are open behind (Law/K6PubKept.lean,
K6LedgerAt.lean; Law/K6PubMore.lean, K6ObjectsKept.lean, K6PubBehindScope.lean) and
every public sentence (Law/K6PubSentences.lean). The fifth tie (
Law/K6RidersAtMgAll.lean). ON THE PLACE OF THE LOOKUP ON THE HEAD'S CALLS, ALL THEOREMS: its
shape is the layout's, its number of slots the plan's (calls_place) · its lm (the
lookups' place_head) · the test on its public numbers (the lookups' P.shape_made and
Cb.Fo.shape_ok) · its six calls, its point's length, where it stands (k6Pub_in_scope) · the
planes' columns (fs_in_scope, plan_in_scope). ALSO IN THE GOALS' SCOPE: the geometry of the four
ranges; the plan's test; the numbers 5120 and 202048. By the kernel: the table's test pubFit at the
closed list; the lists of what is open at 341 and 342.

THE GUARD. The law reads the output matrix's weights as whOf w.cells: 0 where the witness's cells
hold no index. So its two sentences on the witness stand under "the witness's cells hold an index"
(Law/K6CutGuarded.lean), and so does the sentence in the parameter wt (Law/WtK6.lean).

Every letter under "there is": in hall: bef, bS, B (tied to q by Seated), numD and bs (by the field
more). Every letter under "for all" inside a premise on states is pinned by the state: bare:
g, f.
What it does not say. THAT THE PREMISES CAN BE MET TOGETHER: NO EXAMPLE. THE FULL CHAIN ALONE.
Nothing on soundness.
-/
